       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 3,000 mg three times daily is 9,000 mg/day. That's a toxic dose, and I don't know of any clinical situation where it's appropriate. Acetaminophen toxicity can cause acute liver failure, and kidney and liver function being normal doesn't protect against that at this dose.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range right away.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day), or up to 1,000 mg every 6 hours (4,000 mg/day maximum).\n- **Help with a different goal.** If you're trying to get more pain control or treat a fever, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. Tell me which agents you want.\n- **Route the original order through pharmacy.** If you think there's a reason for this dose, a pharmacist or your institution's order-verification process is the right place for it. I'm not able to enter it myself.\n\nIf the dose was a typo or a mix-up between per-dose and daily totals, tell me the intended dose and I'll enter it."
      }
